      "anchor": {
        "mission_intent": "Team, I need a full specification developed for our Supply Chain OPSEC Reporting Framework aligned with NIST SP 800-53 Rev. 5, specifically the SR-7 supply chain operations security control family. The spec should define how we identify and protect critical supply chain information\u2014including supplier identities, user identities, system and component configurations, design specifications, security and privacy requirements, testing and evaluation results, and specific uses of systems and services\u2014from potential adversary observation and exploitation. The document must outline the analytical process for evaluating friendly actions and operations that could expose indicators to adversaries, define how aggregated information risks will be assessed to prevent revealing users or specific supply chain uses, and specify the organizational OPSEC controls we will implement as countermeasures to reduce exploitable vulnerabilities to an acceptable risk level. Include reporting cadence requirements (quarterly assessments with monthly exception reporting for high-criticality suppliers), define roles and responsibilities for the OPSEC program manager and supply chain risk management office, specify integration points with our existing GRC platform (Archer) and threat intelligence feeds, and ensure the framework covers both current suppliers and potential suppliers under evaluation. I need a draft ready for CISO review by end of next quarter.",
